      "value": "This is a Unity bug that VRChat cannot fix. It is fixed in a future Unity version per Euan's post: \n\n\"This is a unity bug fixed in untiy 2017.3 https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/issues/setting-videoplayer-dot-frame-from-code-offsets-audio\"\n\nI am setting this to \"Under Review\" despite it being a known bug, as it is reliant on a base Unity version upgrade.\n\nPlease note that in our testing, high CPU usage will aggravate your A/V desync (high numbers of users in a room, alt-tabbing between applications while watching a video, etc)",
